  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Right Here, Right Now 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Right Here Right Now 2 (RHRN2) builds on the successes of its predecessor Right Here Right Now (2016-2020) funded by the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The new partnership, RHRN2 (2021-2025) consists of consortium partners Rutgers (lead), AMPF, ARROW, CHOICE for Youth and Sexuality, RHU, and RNW Media, and technical partners Dance4Life and IPPF AR.The strategic objective of RHRN2 is for young people in all their diversity to enjoy their sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) in gender-just societies. By placing young people at the forefront of the partnership, RHRN2 seeks:&#x2022; to increase public support for SRHR;&#x2022; to improve policies and laws; and&#x2022; to strengthen civil society.CHOICE is the youth-led partner in the consortium of the RHRN2 partnership and focuses on meaningful youth participation in decision-making and youth-led advocacy on youth&apos;s SRHR and bodily autonomy.</narrative>
  </description>
